From: System Electronics
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 12:30:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] drm/panel: waveshare-dsi: log which panel the device tree selected

The MCU exposes no ID or version register, and no public register map
exists for it. The driver therefore cannot detect which panel is
physically attached, and put in front of the wrong one it "succeeds" and
drives it at the wrong resolution, producing a broken image with no error
anywhere in the log.

With more than one device tree shipping this driver, that is the trap
waiting for whoever selects the wrong one. Failing cleanly is not
possible, so state at probe what the device tree asked for.

---
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-waveshare-dsi.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-waveshare-dsi.c
@@ -443,6 +443,7 @@
 		.node = NULL,
 	};
 	const struct ws_panel_data *_ws_panel_data;
+	const char *compat = NULL;
 	int ret;
 
 	ts = devm_kzalloc(dev, sizeof(*ts), GFP_KERNEL);
@@ -461,6 +462,13 @@
 
 	ts->i2c = i2c;
 
+	/* The MCU has no ID register: log what the device tree selected. */
+	of_property_read_string(dev->of_node, "compatible", &compat);
+	dev_info(dev, "Waveshare panel '%s' at %pOF: %ux%u@%u, %d lane(s)\n",
+		 compat ? compat : "unknown", dev->of_node,
+		 ts->mode->hdisplay, ts->mode->vdisplay,
+		 drm_mode_vrefresh(ts->mode), _ws_panel_data->lanes);
+
 	ws_panel_i2c_write(ts, 0xc0, 0x01);
 	ws_panel_i2c_write(ts, 0xc2, 0x01);
 	ws_panel_i2c_write(ts, 0xac, 0x01);
